From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:43:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 154/154] PC5: fewer "too many open files": files opened for writing,
 locked files and files bound to a completion port are parked, many folders
 can be watched, and an open that runs out says why (Wine patches 1022 to
 1025)

A PS5 title can hold about 249 open files. 0993 parks read-only files past a budget, but not a file opened for writing, a locked one or one bound to a completion port, and every watched folder kept one, so games holding many of those still ran out: modded Minecraft's SQLite databases (Distant Horizons), Project Zomboid watching the 1704 folders of its media tree as Java does, a game reading through a completion port. Those files are now parked too (1023, 1025), descriptors handed to a program uncached are lent until it closes them so a parked file never saves a stale position (1025, a new server request kept last), a parked folder shares the files' budget and one timer polls all watched folders within a time budget (1024), and an open that still runs out logs what holds the descriptors (1022). PC5's own rule from 0994 stays: a parked file or folder opened again under another number by its file system is taken and logged. From leolobato/prospero-win's 1002, 1009, 1019 and 1021.
